DO Using only the user's request after /inux pr, set mode to "prepare" for creating or drafting
    a PR, including a target-only request, "refine" for editing or improving its title or
    description, "explain" for explaining, or "publish" for an explicit publication request.
    Classify meaning, not exact keywords; preserve the request for the selected route.
    Set mode to NULL for missing, unsupported, conflicting, or ambiguous intent. Never infer
    publication or choose a partial route for multiple requested actions.
    Do not inspect projects, read task files, or call tools to classify intent.

IF mode == NULL:
    STOP "Error: cannot classify PR request. Usage: /inux pr [request]. Request prepare, refine, explain, or publish; for example: /inux pr improve the title."

CHECK mode is one of "prepare"/"publish"/"refine"/"explain".

IF mode == "publish":
    CHECK The developer explicitly requested publishing this PR.

DO Resolve absolute project, ticket_path, and pr_path; require ticket.md/pr.md (not estimate.md),
    without reset/full reads. Read ticket heading as ticket_id; reject supplied-ID mismatch. Batch
    independent reads/checks, retain exits, and reuse unchanged evidence/instructions.

DO Resolve project AGENTS.md rules/checks and explicit user naming overrides; old history never
    overrides.

IF mode == "prepare":
    USE pr/prepare.flow

IF mode == "refine":
    USE pr/refine.flow

IF mode == "explain":
    USE pr/explain.flow

IF mode == "publish":
    USE pr/publish.flow
